- Removed redundant App Store app installs that Fleet had queued for itself on hosts whose upcoming activity queue was not draining, keeping the most recently queued install of each app on each host. This covers both automatic updates and policy automations, which each appended a copy per cycle. Where an install of that app had already been sent to the device, the queued copies are removed and the one in flight is kept. Installs requested from the install button, self-service, or the setup experience are left in place. Because the most recent copy is kept, it now runs after anything that was queued between the duplicates.
